From e02697938d10c216c4009d81b2e3debb1d1e133a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 05:21:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Simplify menus: remove animations, minimize continuous
 processing

- Removed all continuous/infinite animations (pulsing indicators, expanding
  ripples, orbiting background glow + particle field, marquee progress
  gradient) that redrew every frame regardless of user activity
- Converted ~200 tween()/spring()/keyframes() animation specs to instant
  snap() across 41 files (menu expand/collapse, screen fades, dialog
  open/close, button press feedback, nav transitions)
- Disabled default Compose enter/exit animations on AnimatedVisibility/
  Crossfade calls that had none specified explicitly
- Converted smooth-scroll calls (animateScrollTo/animateScrollToItem) to
  instant scrolling across 10 files
- Removed legacy View-system dialog scale/fade animation and activity
  slide transition, pointing them at the existing no_animation resource
- Deleted now-orphaned animation XML resources
- Cleaned up unused imports and dead code left behind by the above
